--- !u!114 &328672697
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 328672696}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 83c90e794281e6c45a7e3be79a668332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::InteriorDialogueManager
  minigameScene: SpotDifference_W2
  returnScene: WorldMap2
  introLines:
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Glad you stopped by. I've got two security alert emails from what looks
      like our IT department.
  - speaker: Player
    text: Two that look the same? One of them is almost certainly a fake.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: That's what I thought. But they both have the company logo and everything.
  - speaker: Player
    text: "Logos are trivial to copy. The differences will be in the details \u2014
      sender domain, link URLs, fine print."
  - speaker: NPC
    text: My staff nearly clicked the link in one of them already.
  - speaker: Player
    text: Then let's go through both carefully and find every mismatch before anyone
      else does.
  winLines:
  - speaker: NPC
    text: "You caught every difference \u2014 even the extra hyphen in the domain
      name!"
  - speaker: Player
    text: That's usually the last thing people check, which is exactly why attackers
      hide it there.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: I'm going to add sender domain verification to our email policy today.
  - speaker: Player
    text: That's one of the best things a small office can do.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: Thank you. I'll brief the whole team this afternoon.
  loseLines:
  - speaker: NPC
    text: "We missed some \u2014 those differences were very subtle."
  - speaker: Player
    text: Corporate phishing emails are the most polished kind. Let's look again.
  - speaker: NPC
    text: "Please \u2014 I need to be sure before I show my team."
  npcName: Mr. Frost
  npcSprite: {fileID: -6881917104480724425, guid: 825603d3841d72249a94145126309c3a, type: 3}
